     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Two controls suffice: mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin. With mfa_dbadmin deployed, auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which come only from auth_dc or auth_adfs. mfa_admin blocks both of those. So no exfiltration target can be reached, even though reach_internal, stolen_admin and stolen_dbadmin (via ciserver) are still obtainable. One control is not enough. Phishing always gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, so pivot_internal works unless segmented, patched_workstation and patched_laptop are all deployed (3 controls). mfa_user has no effect because foothold_workstation always exists. With mfa_admin alone, the ciserver yields stolen_dbadmin and auth_db then works. With mfa_dbadmin alone, auth_dc leads to admin_dc, which lets auth_db through. No single patch blocks the chain, because the escalations can use stolen_admin instead.\"}"
    }
   ],
